stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> QUEUED: a flow creates the command, type supported by the model
    QUEUED --> SERVED: device poll, one in flight per device user, creation order
    SERVED --> SUCCEEDED: result success, id and serial match
    SERVED --> FAILED: result failure, or no result within the source timeout
    FAILED --> QUEUED: source retry interval elapses, below the source ceiling
    FAILED --> SUCCEEDED: late success for an earlier attempt
    QUEUED --> SUCCEEDED: late success for an earlier attempt of a re-queued command
    QUEUED --> SUPERSEDED: later update for the same device user, no delete between
    QUEUED --> EXPIRED: clock set unserved past its time to live, or replaced
    QUEUED --> CANCELLED: device decommissioned, delete types excepted
    SUCCEEDED --> [*]
    SUPERSEDED --> [*]
    EXPIRED --> [*]
    CANCELLED --> [*]
    note right of QUEUED
        Delete-user and delete-template are never
        superseded, expired or cancelled.
        A suspended device is served deletes only.
    end note
    note right of FAILED
        At the source ceiling the erasure item
        becomes EXHAUSTED or the provisioning
        is marked pending. A punch is never blocked.
    end note
